# HSEQ Nova — law-first development

## Ground rule

Before any new function, field or module is implemented, check what UK law and HSE guidance actually require. Do not assume or guess — find the legal basis.

## Primary sources

| Law / guidance | Area | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Health and Safety at Work etc. Act 1974 (HSWA) s.2 | Employer duties, written policy (≥5 employees) | Statement + organisation + arrangements |
| Management of Health and Safety at Work Regulations 1999 (MHSWR) | Suitable and sufficient risk assessments | Competent person |
| RIDDOR 2013 | Reportable deaths, specified injuries, over-7-day, disease, dangerous occurrences | Immediate / 10-day / 15-day |
| Social Security (Claims and Payments) Regulations 1979 | Accident book (≥10 employees; digital is lawful) | Keep 3 years |
| COSHH 2002 | Hazardous substances assessments and health records | Health records 40 years |
| CDM 2015 | Construction duty holders, CPP, F10, H&S File | Client, PD, PC |
| Regulatory Reform (Fire Safety) Order 2005 | Responsible person, drills, fire risk assessment | |
| PIDA 1998 | Whistleblowing | |
| SRSCWR 1977 / HSCER 1996 | Safety representatives and consultation | |
| UK GDPR / DPA 2018 | Personal data, accident records | ICO |
| ISO 45001 / 14001 / 9001 | Management systems | International |

## How to add features

1. Identify the legal area.
2. Look up the concrete duty on HSE.gov.uk or legislation.gov.uk.
3. Define mandatory fields from the duty.
4. Define optional fields.
5. Implement validation that mirrors the duty. Cite the section in comments.

## Incident types (RIDDOR, not AML)

- Death — report without delay
- Specified injury — 10 days
- Over-seven-day injury — 15 days
- Occupational disease
- Dangerous occurrence
- Near miss (not RIDDOR; keep in accident book / incident module)

## When unsure

Search `hse.gov.uk` and `legislation.gov.uk`. Always cite the regulation in field descriptions that are legally required.
